; fas9_surfaces.scr - facit script of step 9.16 (F9.17 NURBSURFACE, F9.18 the isolines of the 2004 surfaces). Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_surfaces.scr
; It starts from AutoCAD's own acad.dwt (a new empty drawing) and uses plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (the core has none).
; SURFACEASSOCIATIVITY 0: a surface is then the entity alone (the associative framework is fas9_assoc_core.scr's). Every
; surface is drawn in a cell of its own (120 units), so a window selects it and nothing else.
;
; Files (acad_<version>_dxf_<theme>[_<change>][_bin].dxf, R12 and 2000 ... 2018; the core cannot save R13/R14):
;   surfaces_analytic   planes (6 + 6, 3 + 9, 1 + 1, 13 + 2 isolines), a cylinder, a cone, elliptic cylinders, spheres, tori and extruded arcs
;                       whole and partial (the analytic faces of F9.18: plane, cone/cylinder, sphere, torus), revolved lines
;   surfaces_spline     extruded splines and polylines, lofts of splines (one and several knot spans, closed), a swept circle, a revolved spline
;   surfaces_trim       planes and a cylinder before and after SURFTRIM: a round hole, a hole that touches an isoline, a rectangular hole,
;                       a bite out of an edge (face loops, holes, a reversed loop)
;   surfaces_nurbs      before and after CONVTONURBS of a plane, a cylinder, a cone, a sphere, a torus, a loft, a revolved line and a swept
;                       line (the NURBSURFACE of F9.17), then the same shapes made in SURFACEMODELINGMODE 1
;   surfaces_transform  a loft, a cylinder and a torus moved, rotated, scaled and mirrored, one change per file
;
; What AutoCAD 2025's core cannot do, and is therefore "ej testat" (plan 2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md, F9.17, F9.18): a change of
; a surface's own isoline counts after it was made (71 and 72 are the SURFU and SURFV of its making: they vary between the
; surfaces drawn, they are not changed afterwards; the properties palette is the only other way and the core has none), R13/R14.
